 "productionNotes": "Sources do not agree on a single BNR32 total. The figure most often repeated in English-language references and enthusiast media is 43,934 (attributed to GT-R Magazine); Wikipedia and several buyer's guides give 43,937. An independent chassis-number analysis published by GTR USA arrives at 42,956, and archived GT-R Registry data at 43,896, leaving roughly 1,000 cars unaccounted for depending on which basis is used; Japanese registration totals for 1989-1994 come to 41,692, with the balance plausibly pre-production, press, export and competition cars. Because no primary Nissan figure is publicly published, no single total is asserted here. Variant sub-figures are better attested but still vary: Nismo (Group A evolution) 560, of which 500 were sold to the public and 60 retained for competition; V-Spec 1,396 or 1,453 depending on source; V-Spec II 1,306 or 1,303; N1 either 118 (pre-V-Spec cars only) or approximately 245 when V-Spec N1 (64) and V-Spec II N1 (63) cars are included, against 228 in the GTR USA tally. Production ran from August 1989 to November 1994. The GT-R was a Japan-market car with one official export exception: 100 Australian-delivered examples supplied in 1991.",
